<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Emile Griffith returns with his care partner for the results of his neuropsychological testing, done a week ago, and of the work-up. He has had three sessions of cognitive processing therapy; he says it is hard to write about the fight but he feels lighter after each session, and the psychologist gives him one-page summaries that his care partner reads with him between sessions. Nightmares come four or five nights a week instead of most nights. He takes sertraline 25 mg each morning without side effects. He has had no falls and no thoughts of suicide. His care partner says he repeats stories less when he is rested. He asked to hear the results with his care partner present. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Neuropsychological testing</td><td>Mild cognitive impairment of frontal-subcortical type; retrieval better with cues; effort valid</td></tr><tr><td>PCL-5</td><td>37, from 41 at intake</td></tr><tr><td>PHQ-9</td><td>8; item 9 scored 0</td></tr><tr><td>Therapy</td><td>Three sessions of cognitive processing therapy</td></tr><tr><td>Physical therapy</td><td>Evaluation booked for next week</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

